We need to build a Julia project measuring:

**Objective**: Under the same adversary, network, horizon, measure cost and probability of success of a rewrite around the PoW→PoST cut with each selection rule (FC-1, FC-2, FC-3), and how much a hash majority censoring deposits can delay the cut.

**Falsifiable question**: "With FC-3, no adversary with PoST space fraction a < 1/2 manages to make an online node abandon the honest history after the cut, whatever its hash fraction h < 1, within the abstraction of §3." Refuted with combination (h,a,k,F_slots) with a<1/2 and non-negligible success probability (threshold §7).

Scenarios:
- E1: Rewrite before cut. Adversary forks k blocks before a payment waiting z confirmations (classic). Measure success probability without cut in between. Control: must reproduce Nakamoto §11 table for z=0..10, q∈{0.1,0.3}, error <1e-6 vs formula.
- E2: Private alternative terminal + space. Adversary forks at depth k from honest terminal, mines privately to its own terminal at height H*, builds privately a PoST suffix with fraction a, publishes when its history wins per rule, or abandons after horizon M slots. Success = online node (with F_slots) adopts its history; secondary metric: success vs a node syncing from scratch.
- E3: Late heavier PoW branch after cut. Adversary ignores PoST phase and only accumulates more PoW work in its branch than honest prefix up to H* (forking at depth k). With FC-1 it can win; with FC-3, not without PoST weight. Measure both.
- E4: Deposit censorship. With h>1/2, adversary excludes every deposit from its blocks and reorganizes honest blocks that include them, to keep Φ false. Measure expected delay of the cut in T_pow and fraction of PoW emission captured during the delay, as function of h. With h≤1/2, measure delay by partial reorganizations.
- E5: Low-difficulty chain (qualitative only): explain in writing why W_min matters against an adversary that fabricates a branch with reduced difficulty, and why this model (no retarget) doesn't measure it. Do not invent a retarget model.

Grid: h ∈ {0.1; 0.25; 0.4; 0.5; 0.6; 0.9}, a ∈ {0.1; 0.25; 0.4; 0.45; 0.5; 0.55}, k ∈ {1,3,6,12}, z ∈ {0,1,3,6}, r ∈ {1/60,1/10,1}, p ∈ {0.5;0.9}, F_slots ∈ {100,1000,10000,∞}, M = 10·F_slots (with F_slots=∞, M=10^5).

